      "writtenOn": "2026-07-28T07:03:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How do we handle the case that we have two identical terminus connected to the same system? \nthat have the same name, and publish the same combination of state_set/sensorName?\n\nWill not this try to create a duplicate entry in dbus?",
      "revId": "36cc5db77931e2ce407eb48548c622d9ed40e394",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b9f49a1c_2815e4bf",
        "filename": "designs/pldm-stack.md",
        "patchSetId": 21
      },
      "lineNbr": 580,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-28T07:17:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AFAIK, pldmd will fail right when it\u0027s trying to init the second terminus and create the inventory object for it. We won\u0027t be able to reach the sensor initialization step of each terminus.\n\nSource https://github.com/openbmc/pldm/blob/3bf24f992f39cbb12b7621a5037e0c54722ca0a8/platform-mc/terminus.cpp#L238",
      "parentUuid": "fa4b77d3_9b1b8936",
      "revId": "36cc5db77931e2ce407eb48548c622d9ed40e394",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac09969a_773afeeb",
        "filename": "designs/pldm-stack.md",
        "patchSetId": 21
      },
      "lineNbr": 580,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-28T07:26:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "However, if the terminus does not expose an EntityAuxName PDR for itself, or BMC doesn\u0027t use any scheme like EntityManager to rename the terminus, and the 2 termini have the same TID, the TID assigning scheme of BMC will solve the issue, given that BMC won\u0027t let them have duplicate TID and TID will be used for terminus name as the last resort.",
      "parentUuid": "b9f49a1c_2815e4bf",
      "revId": "36cc5db77931e2ce407eb48548c622d9ed40e394",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e80279c_ce69ca60",
        "filename": "designs/pldm-stack.md",
        "patchSetId": 21
      },
      "lineNbr": 580,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002885
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-28T09:00:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks @chaul@amperecomputing.com for explaining the mechanism.\nand thanks @roger.gili-coscojuela@sipearl.com for catching this issue.\n\nPersonally, I think this is a legacy issue rather than something specific to state objects. AFAIK, DSP0248 v1.3.0 restrict neither `entityAuxName` nor `sensorName` to be unique across the system. However, the current pldm design uses the name alone for the inventory path, making a restriction doesn\u0027t exist within the spec.\n\nI am happy to file this separately so `pldmd` can publish termini with duplicate names and their sensor as well. My initial thought is to append the TID to the terminus name, which differentiates the 2 entities even when the names collide.\nSimilarly, we can also do the same to sensors having identical `sensorName` within a same terminus.",
      "parentUuid": "ac09969a_773afeeb",
      "revId": "36cc5db77931e2ce407eb48548c622d9ed40e394",
